<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pentathlus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. c. 580 BCE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pentathlus was a Greek leader from Cnidus who, according to Diodorus and Pausanias, led settlers from Cnidus and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhodes">Rhodes</a> to found a colony near Lilybaeum in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a> around 580 BCE. The attempt failed in fighting with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elymians">Elymians</a> of Segesta and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phoenicians">Phoenicians</a>, Pentathlus was killed, and the survivors went on to settle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lipari">Lipari</a>.</p></div>
